      summary: "Puducherry is a four-part union territory — Puducherry and Karaikal on the Coromandel coast, Yanam further north on the Andhra coast and Mahe on the Malabar coast — and its community map follows that geography. It is the only Indian territory with five official languages (Tamil, English, Malayalam, Telugu and French), a legacy of French rule from the seventeenth century to 1954 and of the 1956 Treaty of Cession. That double inheritance also produced a Franco-Tamil creole cuisine and a calendar in which Bastille Day sits beside temple car festivals.",
