      culturalHistory: "Punjab's public culture was shaped by the Sikh Gurus' institutions — the gurdwara, the takhts, and langar, the free kitchen open to all faiths that Guru Nanak established and that today serves on the order of a hundred thousand meals a day at Amritsar. Hola Mohalla, founded by Guru Gobind Singh at Anandpur Sahib, turned a spring festival into a display of martial discipline. Beneath that lies an agrarian society whose harvest joy produced bhangra (men's, to the dhol) and giddha (women's circle dance), which grew into global markers of Punjabi identity.",
