      summary: "West Bengal is a Bengali-majority state with India's second-largest Muslim population share — 27 per cent, about 24.6 million people, at the 2011 Census, overwhelmingly Bengali Muslims — plus 40 notified Scheduled Tribes totalling 52.97 lakh, 5.8 per cent of the state. The Santal are the largest tribe and Toto, Birhor and Lodha are the state's three Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups. Bengali is the official language, and successive amendments to the West Bengal Official Language Act have added Nepali, Urdu, Hindi, Santali, Odia, Punjabi and, in 2018, Kamtapuri, Rajbanshi and Kurmali for official use where those communities are concentrated. Kolkata's Durga Puja was inscribed by UNESCO in 2021.",
